course: dictionary
lesson: 9025
title: Skyscraper: a very tall building
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A skyscraper is a very tall building with many floors, found in a city. You can read the word as sky and scraper: a building so tall it seems to scrape the sky. Words that sound like pictures can help you remember them.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «A penny dropped from a skyscraper slows down in the air and tumbles» tells you it is high up and that you could drop something from its top. «The first skyscraper, built in Chicago in 1885, had about 10 floors» tells you that many floors are part of what makes a skyscraper.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The tallest very tall building with many floors, in a city» in place of «the tallest skyscraper». If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Skyscraper is a noun: one skyscraper, two skyscrapers.
fact: «Skyscraper» means a very tall building with many floors, in a city.
fact: The first skyscraper was built in Chicago in 1885 and had about 10 floors.
fact: The Burj Khalifa in Dubai, opened in 2010, is 828 metres tall.
fact: A skyscraper's strong steel or concrete core and frame carry its weight down to deep foundations.
exercise: «The first skyscraper, built in Chicago in 1885, had about 10 floors.» What is a skyscraper? | *A very tall building with many floors, in a city | A tall tree in a park | A kind of cloud | A small shop on a country lane
exercise: «The Burj Khalifa in Dubai, opened in 2010, is 828 metres tall.» Which city is it in? | Sydney | *Dubai | New York | Chicago
exercise: «A skyscraper's strong steel or concrete core and frame carry the weight down to deep foundations.» Find and copy one building material. | frame | foundations | *steel | weight
test: «The largest known cave passage is Son Doong in Vietnam, big enough to hold a city block with skyscrapers.» What does skyscrapers mean in this sentence? | Steep hills covered in trees | Bridges over a river | *Very tall buildings with many floors, in a city | A small house with one floor
test: «Skyscraper lifts move several metres a second, and the fastest in the world travel at around 20 metres a second.» About how fast do the fastest skyscraper lifts travel? | About 2000 metres a second | About 200 metres a second | *About 20 metres a second | About 2 metres a second
exam: «The first skyscraper, built in Chicago in 1885, had about 10 floors.» Which swap keeps the meaning? | A river bridge | *A very tall building with many floors | A grassy hill | A short bus
